      "text": "I changed `src/` to follow SPEC.md, and the public tests still pass (5 pass, 0 fail). I didn't add tests for the new behaviours, so the fixes below are untested.\n\n**`src/inventory.ts`**\n- Receiving into an existing lot id now adds to its quantity instead of replacing it.\n- Available stock now ignores expired lots.\n- Lots with the same expiry are now used in id order.\n\n**`src/orders.ts`**\n- An order that can't be filled in full now releases anything it had partly reserved.\n- Two lines for the same sku no longer overwrite each other's reservation.\n\n**`src/backorder.ts`**\n- Backorders are retried in the order they were placed, not smallest first.\n- Cancelled orders are skipped and dropped from the queue.\n\n**`src/warehouse.ts`**\n- Shipping is refused when the quantity exceeds what is still reserved for that sku.\n- Cancelling releases only the reserved units, not the shipped ones. It also removes the order from the backorder queue and retries the remaining backorders.\n- Returns skip units that were already returned, so the latest shipped units still come back first.",
